A||||15||sjp777||Why is the 88 V6 such a dog?||||5||
Z||000000||sjp777||04-14-2001||11:47 AM||||Does anyone know why the V6 in the 88's the worst performing HP wise of the bunch? I have heard that Pontiac detuned the 88's a bit for emissions purposes. Does anyone know what they did and how to undo it?<P>Before I had my 88, I had an 86se V6 that would easily chirp the tires on a hard shift from 1st to 2nd. I've never been able to get the 88 to do that, even with the K&N and power pulley that the 86 didn't have.<P>Is it all in the chip, and can I swap an 86 chip into the 88 ecm?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||pHoOl||04-14-2001||01:14 PM||||It's interesting, cause i hear that the 88 is a dog and the 85GT is the fastest.  So one day my buddy and i had a little race, him in his 85GT 4spd, and me in my 88GT auto, and we were pretty much even.  maybe he wasn't trying, but i was still kinda shocked.  <P>Anybody know of ways to make the 88V6 a lil faster?  i'd like get some better off the line power.  Thinking about the cold air induction, but not sure how much this will gain me.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||04-14-2001||01:14 PM||||88 are heavyest model year inproved sept.<BR>and stiffend frame do add mass to car.<BR>but diffret cars and motors may vary more than that in same year.<BR>motor is all most same ecpt ballance and oil pump+pan and covers that don't matter for HP.<BR>tune up time?? I don't think older stock comp. will help to add power.is cat good??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||04-14-2001||02:53 PM||||The only weight difference between early cars and '88s is the front suspension crossmember/subframe and assembly, which is about twice as heavy for '88's as it is for early cars.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||04-14-2001||03:14 PM||||The 85 GT was rated at 140 hp. 86-88 were rated at 135 hp. Possible different ECMs, different fuel maps etc. Ive heard a variety of different reasons why (insurance, reevaluations of testing, etc) but Ive never heard of the 88s in particular being dogs. If anything, the internal balancing of the crankshaft was the only thing that was different from this V6. <P>According to the 22P Parts book the 85 is the only year listed with its own ECM number. 86-88 have the same number for the ECM. (Page 3-45) Further break down shows a multitude of different numbers for the CALPAKs depenedent on the year of the Fiero, engine, tranny and if it was a California car or not.)<P>I agree with ray b. You could easily take two cars of the same year and have different results. It depends on the tolerances built into the engine, how well the engine is broken in (mileage, highway use, street use) how well its been tuned up and the condition of the clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||04-14-2001||03:14 PM||||ve a different exhaust and cat for 88.  Thats the most likely spot for any loss of power, although I haven't really noticed much of a difference between the years.  I certainly wouldn't call an 88 V6 Fiero a dog.  But if you just have to have more power, find yourself a 3.4L Camaro motor!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||sjp777||04-14-2001||03:35 PM||||The cat is long gone. (actually in a box in my garage for emission tests) and I never let it get to the point where it needs a tune up. Maybe i just got lucky with the 86. But anyway, 135 hp is less than half what I want. 3.4 just ain't gonna cut it. I see an LS1 in my future.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||6
Z||000007||FieroSTETZ||04-15-2001||10:51 AM||||wherever you got the hp specs, see what RPM they were both putting out at, GM tested the 2 at different rpm's, something to do with emissions, there is no actual difference in hp. its like in the 60's they would say 250 hp on a 400 hp car, but for insurance||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mr.Frosty||04-15-2001||11:18 AM||||When I talked to Fiero Phil one time he told me the same thing,that they claimed lower HP numbers for the emmisions Gestapo.The motor was actually the same,if not more improved(internally balanced)All I know is when Road and Track tested the fieros throughout the years the Formula was the fastest at 7.0 to 7.5 seconds to 60mph.It's on the video that FOCOA sells that was produced by Road and Track in the 80's.Most V-6 fieros to that point in time would hit it at 8.5.I can't remember off hand,but I think the 86SE or one of the SE years was also a hot runner as it had different gearing that helped it with low speed acceleration.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-ForSale <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||6
