Z||000014||TwisT||04-16-2001||09:07 AM||||Correct me if I'm wrong (it's happened before...  lol),  but would the main decrease in acceleration in the '88 be from the not only the above factors,  but more importantly,  transmission drive ratio?<P>I've had an '85 GT,  '86 GT and currently an '88 GT.  Fastest of the bunch?  The '85.  Reason?  Well,  '85's ARE slightly lighter.  But I'm thinking the big reason is the different drive ratio in the tranny's.  I remember chirping the tires through 3rd gear in that car...<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||04-16-2001||02:38 PM||||im with the statement that 2 similar cars will run completely different. I had 2 Lincoln Mark III's same exact car 460 4bbl, same equipment, even same color in and out. Both rated at 425 hp. Both ran and started perfectly. roughly same miles. One would haul like a rail dragster, other was more like a bus. Never found anything different spec wise, same compression, timing, gearing. I gave up.||||reg||1
